    "senderName": "NWS Hanford CA",
    "headline": "Winter Weather Advisory issued October 21 at 4:35AM PDT until October 22 at 11:00AM PDT by NWS Hanford CA",
    "description": "* WHAT...There is an 70% chance of 4 inches or more of snow along the\nTioga Pass and highway 120. There is a 60-80% chance for four\ninches or more of snow above 8,000 feet in Tulare, Madera, and\nFresno Counties.\n\n* WHERE...Above 8,000 feet in the Sierra Nevada.\n\n* WHEN...From 11 AM this morning to 11 AM PDT Thursday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Roads, and especially bridges and overpasses, will likely\nbecome slick and hazardous.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Snowfall will affect traffic across Tioga\nHighway/Pass.",
    "instruction": "Be prepared for slippery roads. Slow down and use caution while\ndriving. If you are going outside, watch your first few steps taken\non stairs, sidewalks, and driveways. These surfaces could be icy and\nslippery, increasing your risk of a fall and injury.",
